s://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","name":"writer","text":"Writer","type":"certification"}],"city_name":"Minnesota","comment_count":0,"comment_user_count":0,"content":"\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIn southeast Minnesota, there's a 42-mile path that follows a scenic river through small towns and beautiful bluff country. The Root River State Trail offers one of the best places in Minnesota to bike, walk, or spend a weekend outdoors.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe trail is paved and mostly flat, making it easy for cyclists of different skill levels to ride. That's important because this area, called Bluff Country, is actually quite hilly with steep slopes throughout the region. But the trail itself was built on an old railroad line, so \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.exploreminnesota.com/article/ride-root-river-trail-through-southeast-minnesota\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eengineers designed it to be gentle and manageable\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e .\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe trail winds through small towns that have become popular destinations because of the pathway. These towns include Fountain, Harmony, Lanesboro, Houston, Peterson, Preston, Rushford, and Whalan. Each town has its own character and offers different things to visitors.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cfigure\u003e\u003cdiv data-editornodeinfo=\"%7B%22type%22%3A%22editor-image-node%22%2C%22imageUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.prt.news%2F30e9c7a0d5cf6cd467b3d07be63eef54.blob%22%2C%22imageCaption%22%3A%22%22%2C%22creditText%22%3A%22DayTripper%22%2C%22creditUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fdaytripper28.com%2Fthe-root-river-trail%2F%22%2C%22imagePlatform%22%3A%22SELF_UPLOAD%22%2C%22imageOriginalWidth%22%3A768%2C%22imageOriginalHeight%22%3A576%7D\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image-wrap\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image\"\u003e\u003cimg class=\"\" src=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?type=thumbnail_580x000\u0026amp;url=2O2jUY_1CZzmTnT00\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-credit-text=\"DayTripper\" data-credit-url=\"https://daytripper28.com/the-root-river-trail/\" data-image-platform=\"SELF_UPLOAD\" data-image-original-width=\"768\" data-image-original-height=\"576\" alt=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?url=2O2jUY_1CZzmTnT00\" width=\"768\" height=\"576\" \u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-introduction-wrap\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"photo-by\"\u003ePhoto by\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"credit-text\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://daytripper28.com/the-root-river-trail/\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eDayTripper\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLanesboro stands out for its art scene. The town has galleries, shops, and cozy bed-and-breakfasts where visitors can stay overnight. Many people use Lanesboro as their home base when spending multiple days on the trail .\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ePeterson showcases Norwegian heritage, reflecting the history of people who settled in this region generations ago. Rushford features a restored historic depot that now houses a museum and rest area for trail visitors. Whalan, a tiny village, has gained attention for a popular pie shop that cyclists stop at to refuel during their rides.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAlong the path, riders see the Root River flowing nearby, railroad bridges crossing overhead, and rock walls that were blasted out when the railroad was first built. The landscape changes throughout the 42 miles, keeping the experience interesting.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eTrail towns offer \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://daytripper28.com/the-root-river-trail/\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003epractical amenities too\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e. You'll find campgrounds where you can pitch a tent, restaurants for meals, and shops selling items you might need. This infrastructure makes it realistic to spend several days biking the entire trail.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe Root River State Trail represents something important about Minnesota's outdoor recreation. The state has over \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.exploreminnesota.com/outdoors/biking/best-paved-bike-trails\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e4,000 miles of paved trails\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e, and many were created from old railroad lines. These \"rail-to-trail\" projects transformed unused transportation routes into recreation paths that benefit communities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWhether you're an experienced cyclist or just want a peaceful place to walk and enjoy nature, the Root River State Trail delivers. The combination of a manageable path, charming towns, and river views makes it worth the trip to southeast Minnesota.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cstyle style=\"display: none\"\u003e.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol1 {padding: 0 0 0 20px !important;margin: 0 0 24px 0 !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol2 {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;list-style-type: lower-al