their accounts by showing some writing experience on other platforms.","es_description":"Usuarios en el Programa de Colaboradores de NewsBreak que han verificado sus cuentas mostrando algo de experiencia en redacción en otras plataformas.","light_color":"#FF5A5A","light_icon":"https://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","name":"writer","text":"Writer","type":"certification"}],"city_name":"Minneapolis, Minnesota","comment_count":2,"comment_user_count":0,"content":"\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMarrow restaurant, a fine-dining spot known for its French technique and seasonal menus, has closed its doors after three years of operation in Minnesota. The closure reflects challenges facing upscale restaurants across the country right now.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMarrow specialized in what's called \"ingredient-driven\" cooking, which means the chef focuses on high-quality, fresh ingredients and changes the menu based on what's available during each season. The restaurant used classic French cooking methods to prepare dishes that drew serious food lovers. According to \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.kttc.com/2026/05/28/marrow-restaurant-closes-its-doors-after-three-years/\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003enews reports from Minnesota\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e, the owners cited changing dining habits and rising costs as reasons for closing.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cfigure\u003e\u003cdiv data-editornodeinfo=\"%7B%22type%22%3A%22editor-image-node%22%2C%22imageUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.prt.news%2F4a072cabc23a5a7b65054edac237e2fa.blob%22%2C%22imageCaption%22%3A%22%22%2C%22creditText%22%3A%22Marrow%20%7C%20Facebook%22%2C%22creditUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fphoto.php%3Ffbid%3D1559424816182621%26set%3Da.505879124870534%26type%3D3%26ref%3Dembed_post%22%2C%22imagePlatform%22%3A%22SELF_UPLOAD%22%2C%22imageOriginalWidth%22%3A1242%2C%22imageOriginalHeight%22%3A1242%7D\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image-wrap\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image\"\u003e\u003cimg class=\"\" src=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?type=thumbnail_580x000\u0026amp;url=4YCb1R_1CZzQwR600\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-credit-text=\"Marrow | Facebook\" data-credit-url=\"https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=1559424816182621\u0026amp;set=a.505879124870534\u0026amp;type=3\u0026amp;ref=embed_post\" data-image-platform=\"SELF_UPLOAD\" data-image-original-width=\"1242\" data-image-original-height=\"1242\" alt=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?url=4YCb1R_1CZzQwR600\" width=\"1242\" height=\"1242\" \u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-introduction-wrap\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"photo-by\"\u003ePhoto by\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"credit-text\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=1559424816182621\u0026amp;set=a.505879124870534\u0026amp;type=3\u0026amp;ref=embed_post\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eMarrow | Facebook\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eRunning a fine-dining restaurant is expensive. Restaurants need to pay for premium ingredients, trained chefs, skilled servers, and elegant dining spaces. These costs add up quickly. When fewer people come to eat, the money coming in doesn't cover all those expenses.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe closure of Marrow happens as the restaurant industry faces several pressures. Labor costs have increased, food prices have risen, and some customers have changed how they spend money on dining out. The \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.startribune.com/restaurant-roll-call-the-latest-closings-and-openings-in-the-twin-cities/510576451\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStar Tribune\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e has reported on multiple restaurant changes happening across the Twin Cities in 2026.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eInterestingly, the same year Marrow closed, the Michelin Guide announced it would rate \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.startribune.com/after-years-of-speculation-michelin-is-finally-coming-to-minneapolis/601663256\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinneapolis restaurants\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e. The Michelin Guide is famous worldwide for rating restaurants, and having it evaluate Minneapolis restaurants is a big deal for the city. However, this new attention also highlights how competitive and difficult the restaurant business has become.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe closure of Marrow is part of a larger story in Minnesota. Some beloved restaurants have shut down while new ones open, and restaurant owners continue adapting to an uncertain future. The Twin Cities food scene remains active with new restaurants planning to open, but established places like Marrow show that even quality restaurants face real challenges.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFor food lovers who enjoyed Marrow's French-influenced cooking, the closure marks the end of a dining experience. For the restaurant industry, it's a reminder that running a fine-dining establishment requires more than good food and skilled chefs.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cstyle style=\"display: none\"\u003e.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol1 {padding: 0 0