daytrippe_8cf99","offline_mode_disabled":false,"origin_view_type":"web","original_url":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/165062113?sig=0F4A157E0120482898B57C7DDC453243","picked_location":{"address":"Minnesota, USA","coord":"46.729553,-94.6859","displayName":"Minnesota","id":"ChIJmwt4YJpbWE0RD6L-EJvJogI","name":"Minnesota","type":"place_id"},"post_category":{},"post_id":165062113,"post_publish_time":0,"referer":"https://www.newsbreakapp.com","scope":0,"scope_web":0,"share_count":0,"show_as_bloom_ads":false,"source":"DayTripper","summary":"On a humid summer day in 1931, a highway construction crew near Pelican Rapids made a discovery that would rewrite Minnesota's ancient history. As workers graded a frost-heave bump in the road, a road grader suddenly hit something hard—a human skull, empty-eyed and impossibly old.","tagline":"Writer","text_category":{"first_cat":{"Science":0.62035087771483},"second_cat":{"Science_Other":0.62035087771483}},"title":"When Minnesota's Oldest Resident Was Mistaken for a Man","unified_category":"Science","up":7,"url":"https://h5.newsbreakapp.com/mp/1CT2qVit?cv=\u0026platform=2","url_before_mp_full_article":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/165062113?sig=0F4A157E0120482898B57C7DDC453243","video_category":{},"video_metadata":{"default_cover_with_play_icon_cdn_url":"","default_first_frame_cdn_url":""},"viewType":"web","vote":0},{"ai_summary":"","amp":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164922149?sig=39A431E501FA5E00E8F0F6BB39316C4F","audio_file":"","audio_length_sec":0,"canonical_url":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164922149?sig=39A431E501FA5E00E8F0F6BB39316C4F","certifications_badges":[{"dark_color":"#FF5A5A","dark_icon":"https://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","description":"Users in NewsBreak’s Contributor Program who have verified their accounts by showing some writing experience on other platforms.","es_description":"Usuarios en el Programa de Colaboradores de NewsBreak que han verificado sus cuentas mostrando algo de experiencia en redacción en otras plataformas.","light_color":"#FF5A5A","light_icon":"https://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","name":"writer","text":"Writer","type":"certification"}],"city_name":"Minneapolis, Minnesota","comment_count":0,"comment_user_count":0,"content":"\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eIf you love soccer and want to experience the excitement of the FIFA World Cup 2026 with thousands of other fans, Minnesota United is bringing the action directly to downtown Minneapolis. From Now through June 27, the Soccer Celebration at Peavey Plaza will show live \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.mnufc.com/news/minnesota-united-announces-soccer-celebration-for-summer-2026\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWorld Cup\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e matches on a giant outdoor screen.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe event is located at Peavey Plaza, right next to Brit's Pub between South 11th and South 12th Street on Nicollet Mall. It's in the \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.mnufc.com/soccercelebration/\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003emiddle of downtown\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e, so it's easy to get to.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eBest of all, \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.minneapolis.org/blog/where-to-watch-soccer/\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eadmission is free\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e. You do need to claim free tickets through SeatGeek before you go, since the space has limited capacity each day. The tickets are first-come, first-served.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWhat makes this different from watching at home? There's a live DJ keeping the energy up between plays. Minnesota United players and \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.mnufc.com/soccercelebration/what-to-expect\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003especial guests sometimes show up\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e. Food carts from local vendors will be on-site, so you can grab a meal while you watch. There's also the Black and Blue Truck selling Minnesota United gear and official World Cup merchandise from Fanatics.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cfigure\u003e\u003cdiv data-editornodeinfo=\"%7B%22type%22%3A%22editor-image-node%22%2C%22imageUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.prt.news%2F255b3f601e2963f7eb66bbcfe325aa5b.blob%22%2C%22imageCaption%22%3A%22%22%2C%22creditText%22%3A%22Photo%20by%20Emilio%20Garcia%20on%20Unsplash%22%2C%22creditUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Funsplash.com%2F%40piensaenpixel%3Futm_source%3DNewsbreak%26utm_medium%3Dreferral%22%2C%22imagePlatform%22%3A%22UNSPLASH%22%2C%22imageOriginalWidth%22%3A1080%2C%22imageOriginalHeight%22%3A631%7D\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image-wrap\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image\"\u003e\u003cimg class=\"\" src=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?type=thumbnail_580x000\u0026amp;url=1CNjy0_1CQsQ2IV00\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-credit-text=\"Photo by Emilio Garcia on Unsplash\" data-credit-url=\"https://unsplash.com/@piensaenpixel?utm_source=Newsbreak\u0026amp;utm_medium=referral\" data-image-platform=\"UNSPLASH\" data-image-original-width=\"1080\" data-image-original-height=\"631\" alt=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?url=1CNjy0_1CQsQ2IV00\" width=\"1080\" height=\"631\" \u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-introduction-wrap\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"photo-by\"\u003ePhoto by\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"credit-text\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://unsplash.com/@piensaenpixel?utm_source=Newsbreak\u0026amp;utm_medium=referral\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eEmilio Garcia\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cspan class=\"text-on\"\u003eon\u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://unsplash.com/?utm_source=Newsbreak\u0026amp;utm_medium=referral\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"link-unsplash-official\"\u003eUnsplash\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe main screen is set up in Peavey Plaza, which is an outdoor sunken plaza in front of Orchestra Hall. It's surrounded by stairs and landscaping. There are no chairs, but you can bring blankets to sit on. Just know that views from the stairs might get blocked depending on where you sit.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe World Cup happens every four years, and the 2026 tournament is a big deal. Having a free, outdoor viewing space in the middle of the city means soccer fans don't have to crowd into bars or pay for a ticket to join the celebration. Whether you're a hardcore soccer fan or just curious about the World Cup, Peavey Plaza is worth checking out.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cstyle style=\"display: none\"\u003e.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol1 {padding: 0 0 0 20px !important;margin: 0 0 24px 0 !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol2 {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;list-style-type: lower-alpha !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}html body.post #content-div .content ol li ol {margin: 0 !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol3 {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;list-style-type: lower-roman !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol4 {padding: 0;margin: 0;list-style-type: upper-roman !important;list-style-position: