":"ChIJmwt4YJpbWE0RD6L-EJvJogI","name":"Minnesota","type":"place_id"},"post_category":{},"post_id":164922149,"post_publish_time":0,"referer":"https://www.newsbreakapp.com","scope":0,"scope_web":0,"share_count":0,"show_as_bloom_ads":false,"source":"DayTripper","summary":"If you love soccer and want to experience the excitement of the FIFA World Cup 2026 with thousands of other fans, Minnesota United is bringing the action directly to downtown Minneapolis. From Now through June 27, the Soccer Celebration at Peavey Plaza will show live World Cup matches on a giant outdoor screen.","tagline":"Writer","text_category":{"first_cat":{"Sports":0.7608425664067093},"second_cat":{"Sports_Soccer":0.826746066639948},"third_cat":{"Sports_Soccer_MLS":0.580017054428433}},"title":"Free World Cup Watch Party at Peavey Plaza: Minnesota United Soccer Celebration","unified_category":"Sports","up":2,"url":"https://h5.newsbreakapp.com/mp/1CQsQ2IV?cv=\u0026platform=2","url_before_mp_full_article":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164922149?sig=39A431E501FA5E00E8F0F6BB39316C4F","video_category":{},"video_metadata":{"default_cover_with_play_icon_cdn_url":"","default_first_frame_cdn_url":""},"viewType":"web","vote":0},{"ai_summary":"","amp":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164919639?sig=A5E08778D34CBDA47C974C4A3C7745B3","audio_file":"","audio_length_sec":0,"canonical_url":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164919639?sig=A5E08778D34CBDA47C974C4A3C7745B3","certifications_badges":[{"dark_color":"#FF5A5A","dark_icon":"https://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","description":"Users in NewsBreak’s Contributor Program who have verified their accounts by showing some writing experience on other platforms.","es_description":"Usuarios en el Programa de Colaboradores de NewsBreak que han verificado sus cuentas mostrando algo de experiencia en redacción en otras plataformas.","light_color":"#FF5A5A","light_icon":"https://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","name":"writer","text":"Writer","type":"certification"}],"city_name":"Minnesota","comment_count":4,"comment_user_count":0,"content":"\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOn June 17, 2010, something dramatic happened in Minnesota's skies. It was a day of powerful storms that would go down in the state's history books as the most active tornado day ever recorded.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThat afternoon and evening, \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.dnr.state.mn.us/climate/journal/tornadoes_100617.html\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e48 tornadoes touched down across Minnesota\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e. This was more tornadoes in a single day than ever before in the state's recorded history. Across four states, the storm system created \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June_2010_Northern_Plains_tornado_outbreak\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e93 tornadoes total\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e and caused serious damage.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe most powerful tornadoes that day were rated as EF4 on the Enhanced Fujita Scale. This means the winds reached speeds over 165 miles per hour—faster than the fastest wind gusts you'd ever see on a normal day. Three of these \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.dnr.state.mn.us/climate/journal/tornadoes_100617.html\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eEF4 tornadoes\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e hit Minnesota, and they were the strongest tornadoes to touch down in the state \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.weather.gov/dlh/10_year_anniversary_of_June_17_2010_tornado_outbreak\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003esince 1967\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e. That's over 40 years of waiting before Minnesota saw tornadoes this powerful again.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eOne of the strongest tornadoes happened near Conger and Albert Lea in southern Minnesota. This tornado lasted 42 minutes and traveled almost \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June_2010_Northern_Plains_tornado_outbreak\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e17 miles\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e across the land. Its winds reached 175 miles per hour, which is incredibly fast. The damage was enormous—about 13.5 million dollars worth of destruction. Sadly, one person lost their life in that tornado, and \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June_2010_Northern_Plains_tornado_outbreak\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e14 others\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e were hurt.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cfigure\u003e\u003cdiv data-editornodeinfo=\"%7B%22type%22%3A%22editor-image-node%22%2C%22imageUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.prt.news%2Fce2cd738d389adc042d7e54afdf93040.blob%22%2C%22imageCaption%22%3A%22%22%2C%22creditText%22%3A%22Photo%20by%20Greg%20Johnson%20on%20Unsplash%22%2C%22creditUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Funsplash.com%2F%40tornadogreg%3Futm_source%3DNewsbreak%26utm_medium%3Dreferral%22%2C%22imagePlatform%22%3A%22UNSPLASH%22%2C%22imageOriginalWidth%22%3A1080%2C%22imageOriginalHeight%22%3A706%7D\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image-wrap\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image\"\u003e\u003cimg class=\"\" src=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?type=thumbnail_580x000\u0026amp;url=3DPCaO_1CQpLKEE00\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-credit-text=\"Photo by Greg Johnson on Unsplash\" data-credit-url=\"https://unsplash.com/@tornadogreg?utm_source=Newsbreak\u0026amp;utm_medium=referral\" data-image-platform=\"UNSPLASH\" data-image-original-width=\"1080\" data-image-original-height=\"706\" alt=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?url=3DPCaO_1CQpLKEE00\" width=\"1080\" height=\"706\" \u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-introduction-wrap\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"photo-by\"\u003ePhoto by\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"credit-text\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://unsplash.com/@tornadogreg?utm_source=Newsbreak\u0026amp;utm_medium=referral\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eGreg Johnson\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan\u003e\u003cspan class=\"text-on\"\u003eon\u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://unsplash.com/?utm_source=Newsbreak\u0026amp;utm_medium=referral\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"link-unsplash-official\"\u003eUnsplash\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eAll across the state that day, people had to take shelter. \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.dnr.state.mn.us/climate/journal/tornadoes_100617.html\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThree people died\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e in Minnesota that day, and the storms caused damage in many communities. The power of these tornadoes showed how strong nature can be.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eScientists were amazed at how many violent tornadoes happened in just 24 hours. The 2010 outbreak had five times as many EF3 and EF4 tornadoes in one day as most other \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/June_2010_Northern_Plains_tornado_outbreak\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003etornado outbreaks\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e in recent years. It remains one of the most active and powerful tornado days in American weather history.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWeather experts still study that June day to learn how such strong storms form. June 17, 2010, is a day Minnesotans remember as a powerful reminder of nature's incredible force.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cstyle style=\"display: none\"\u003e.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol1 {padding: 0 0 0 20px !important;margin: 0 0 24px 0 !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol2 {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;list-style-type: lower-alpha !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}html body.post #content-div .content ol li ol {margin: 0 !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol3 {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;list-style-type: lower-roman !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol4 {padding: 0;margin: 0;list-style-type: upper-roman !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol5 {padding: 0;margin: 0;list-style-type: lower-roman !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;margin-left: 20px !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}@media all and (max-width: 600px) {.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul {margin-left: 14px !important;}}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul li .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul li .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul li::before {display: none !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul {list-style-type: circle !important;margin-left: 0 !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul {list-style-type: square !important;margin-left: 0 !important;}html body.post #content-div .content ul li ul li ul {margin-left: 0 !important;}.ContentEditable__root \u003e ul {margin-bottom: 24px;padding: 0 0 0 20px;}.NBAIEditor_T