,-92.943825","displayName":"Cottage Grove, MN","id":"ChIJv9oMvQHQ94cREkPoM3T8-wo","name":"Cottage Grove","type":"place_id"},"post_category":{},"post_id":164917882,"post_publish_time":0,"referer":"https://www.newsbreakapp.com","scope":0,"scope_web":0,"share_count":4,"show_as_bloom_ads":false,"source":"DayTripper","summary":"Looking for something fun to do this weekend. Check out the Cottage Grove Strawberry Fest, running June 17-20 at Kingston Park, 9195 75th Street South. No entrance fee. Live bands play the main stage Friday and Saturday nights—also free to watch.","tagline":"Writer","text_category":{"first_cat":{"PoliticsGovernment":0.5048805070666441,"Society":0.501674362835172},"second_cat":{"PoliticsGovernment_Municipal":0.5469553906205161,"Society_Other":0.501674362835172},"third_cat":{"PoliticsGovernment_Municipal_Other":0.5469553906205161}},"title":"Cottage Grove Celebrates Summer: Strawberry Fest June 17-20","unified_category":"PoliticsGovernment","up":4,"url":"https://h5.newsbreakapp.com/mp/1CQoVzxq?cv=\u0026platform=2","url_before_mp_full_article":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164917882?sig=28C6349068CF253F1BF3D864FF77AD3C","video_category":{},"video_metadata":{"default_cover_with_play_icon_cdn_url":"","default_first_frame_cdn_url":""},"viewType":"web","vote":0},{"ai_summary":"","amp":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164775400?sig=98B3820D2BFEF428738CD26663DDCD53","audio_file":"","audio_length_sec":0,"canonical_url":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164775400?sig=98B3820D2BFEF428738CD26663DDCD53","certifications_badges":[{"dark_color":"#FF5A5A","dark_icon":"https://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","description":"Users in NewsBreak’s Contributor Program who have verified their accounts by showing some writing experience on other platforms.","es_description":"Usuarios en el Programa de Colaboradores de NewsBreak que han verificado sus cuentas mostrando algo de experiencia en redacción en otras plataformas.","light_color":"#FF5A5A","light_icon":"https://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","name":"writer","text":"Writer","type":"certification"}],"city_name":"Minneapolis, Minnesota","comment_count":0,"comment_user_count":0,"content":"\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGet ready for one of Minneapolis's biggest celebrations of the year. The Stone Arch Bridge Festival is coming to the historic stone bridge this Father's Day weekend, June 20-21, and it's free to attend.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFor 31 years, this festival has drawn thousands of people to the riverfront to see art, listen to live music, and enjoy food from local vendors. The festival runs from 10 a.m. to 7 p.m. on Saturday and 10 a.m. to 5 p.m. on Sunday at the \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://stonearchbridgefestival.com/\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eStone Arch Bridge\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e along W. River Parkway in downtown Minneapolis.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eHere's what makes this festival special: more than 200 artists and food vendors will be there, showing off everything from paintings and sculptures to jewelry and handmade crafts. The bridge itself becomes a gallery where you can walk around, talk to artists about their work, and buy pieces directly from them. Many of the artists are local, meaning you're supporting Minneapolis creators.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cfigure\u003e\u003cdiv data-editornodeinfo=\"%7B%22type%22%3A%22editor-image-node%22%2C%22imageUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.prt.news%2F8d95cfbabd8a25f3022e0fd39085dfd8.blob%22%2C%22imageCaption%22%3A%22%22%2C%22creditText%22%3A%22Stone%20Arch%20Bridge%20Festival%20%7C%20Facebook%22%2C%22creditUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.facebook.com%2Fphoto.php%3Ffbid%3D1339459814892510%26set%3Dpb.100064855111089.-2207520000%26type%3D3%22%2C%22imagePlatform%22%3A%22SELF_UPLOAD%22%2C%22imageOriginalWidth%22%3A2048%2C%22imageOriginalHeight%22%3A1365%7D\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image-wrap\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image\"\u003e\u003cimg class=\"\" src=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?type=thumbnail_580x000\u0026amp;url=2hjE96_1COgvr2O00\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-credit-text=\"Stone Arch Bridge Festival | Facebook\" data-credit-url=\"https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=1339459814892510\u0026amp;set=pb.100064855111089.-2207520000\u0026amp;type=3\" data-image-platform=\"SELF_UPLOAD\" data-image-original-width=\"2048\" data-image-original-height=\"1365\" alt=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?url=2hjE96_1COgvr2O00\" width=\"2048\" height=\"1365\" \u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-introduction-wrap\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"photo-by\"\u003ePhoto by\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"credit-text\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.facebook.com/photo.php?fbid=1339459814892510\u0026amp;set=pb.100064855111089.-2207520000\u0026amp;type=3\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eStone Arch Bridge Festival | Facebook\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe festival isn't just about standing still and looking at art. Multiple stages will have live music throughout both days, from local bands to jazz performances. There's also plenty of food—from traditional festival fare to unique Minnesota restaurants trying out new dishes. And if you're bringing kids, there are family activities and entertainment designed just for them.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWhy call it the Stone Arch Bridge Festival? The bridge itself is iconic. Built in 1883, it's the oldest bridge in Minnesota and a beautiful limestone landmark that's been part of Minneapolis history for over 140 years. The festival celebrates not just the bridge, but the entire riverfront community that makes \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.exploreminnesota.com/event/stone-arch-bridge-festival/11336\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinneapolis special\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFather's Day weekend is the perfect time to bring your family. It's free admission, so you don't have to worry about ticket costs. Whether you're into art, music, food, or just a fun afternoon outside with people you care about, the Stone Arch Bridge Festival has something for everyone.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe festival spans the riverfront area from 11th Avenue South to North 4th Avenue, giving plenty of space to explore. If you go early, you'll avoid crowds. If you go on Sunday afternoon, the festival is a little quieter. Either way, you're looking at a day that celebrates creativity and community right in the heart of Minneapolis.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMark your calendar for June 20-21. Bring the family, bring a friend, or go solo. The Stone Arch Bridge Festival is calling.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cstyle style=\"display: none\"\u003e.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol1 {padding: 0 0 0 20px !important;margin: 0 0 24px 0 !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol2 {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;list-style-type: lower-alpha !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}html body.post #content-div .content ol li ol {margin: 0 !important;}.NBAIEdi