2,"nb_video":{},"nbid":"daytrippe_8cf99","offline_mode_disabled":false,"origin_view_type":"web","original_url":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164775400?sig=98B3820D2BFEF428738CD26663DDCD53","picked_location":{"address":"Minneapolis, MN, USA","coord":"44.977753,-93.26501","displayName":"Minneapolis, MN","id":"ChIJvbt3k5Azs1IRB-56L4TJn5M","name":"Minneapolis","type":"place_id"},"post_category":{},"post_id":164775400,"post_publish_time":0,"referer":"https://www.newsbreakapp.com","scope":0,"scope_web":0,"share_count":10,"show_as_bloom_ads":false,"source":"DayTripper","summary":"Get ready for one of Minneapolis's biggest celebrations of the year. The Stone Arch Bridge Festival is coming to the historic stone bridge this Father's Day weekend, June 20-21, and it's free to attend.","tagline":"Writer","text_category":{"first_cat":{"Lifestyle":0.5063396731186045,"PoliticsGovernment":0.5040130610298119,"Society":0.5668179283337133},"second_cat":{"Lifestyle_Other":0.5063396731186045,"PoliticsGovernment_Other":0.5040130610298119,"Society_Festival":0.5108220697725685},"third_cat":{"Society_Festival_Other":0.5108220697725685}},"title":"Summer Kicks Off: Stone Arch Bridge Festival Returns for Year 31","unified_category":"Society","up":9,"url":"https://h5.newsbreakapp.com/mp/1COgvr2O?cv=\u0026platform=2","url_before_mp_full_article":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164775400?sig=98B3820D2BFEF428738CD26663DDCD53","video_category":{},"video_metadata":{"default_cover_with_play_icon_cdn_url":"","default_first_frame_cdn_url":""},"viewType":"web","vote":0},{"ai_summary":"","amp":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164774947?sig=D719D6DC9A43DF166D57A9826F590D7C","audio_file":"","audio_length_sec":0,"canonical_url":"https://mp.newsbreakapp.com/post/164774947?sig=D719D6DC9A43DF166D57A9826F590D7C","certifications_badges":[{"dark_color":"#FF5A5A","dark_icon":"https://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","description":"Users in NewsBreak’s Contributor Program who have verified their accounts by showing some writing experience on other platforms.","es_description":"Usuarios en el Programa de Colaboradores de NewsBreak que han verificado sus cuentas mostrando algo de experiencia en redacción en otras plataformas.","light_color":"#FF5A5A","light_icon":"https://i.prt.news/t_200_200_ff128e59e44fd908bc949f34bde102c1.png","name":"writer","text":"Writer","type":"certification"}],"city_name":"Minnesota","comment_count":14,"comment_user_count":0,"content":"\u003cbody\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eGas prices are high. Flights are expensive. Hotels cost more than ever. This summer, Americans are making a surprising choice: staying closer to home. And Minnesota is winning because of it.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eFor decades, Americans dreamed of international vacations or trips out west. But in 2026, something shifted. With travel costs soaring, more people are looking at what's nearby instead. That's good news for Minnesota, a state packed with natural beauty, \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.travelandtourworld.com/news/article/nvte2gs5z4in/\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eoutdoor adventures\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e, and interesting cities.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cfigure\u003e\u003cdiv data-editornodeinfo=\"%7B%22type%22%3A%22editor-image-node%22%2C%22imageUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.prt.news%2F4f2232f4cb229a1e494ff5380965e436.blob%22%2C%22imageCaption%22%3A%22%22%2C%22creditText%22%3A%22Jennifer%20A%20Singer%20%7C%20DayTripper%22%2C%22creditUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fdaytripper28.com%2F7-cheap-and-fun-road-trips-to-take-from-minneapolis-this-weekend%2F%22%2C%22imagePlatform%22%3A%22SELF_UPLOAD%22%2C%22imageOriginalWidth%22%3A768%2C%22imageOriginalHeight%22%3A512%7D\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image-wrap\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"editor-image\"\u003e\u003cimg class=\"\" src=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?type=thumbnail_580x000\u0026amp;url=42Iaej_1COgQHSF00\" data-image-caption=\"\" data-credit-text=\"Jennifer A Singer | DayTripper\" data-credit-url=\"https://daytripper28.com/7-cheap-and-fun-road-trips-to-take-from-minneapolis-this-weekend/\" data-image-platform=\"SELF_UPLOAD\" data-image-original-width=\"768\" data-image-original-height=\"512\" alt=\"https://img.particlenews.com/image.php?url=42Iaej_1COgQHSF00\" width=\"768\" height=\"512\" \u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cspan class=\"image-introduction-wrap\"\u003e\u003cspan class=\"photo-by\"\u003ePhoto by\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"credit-text\"\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://daytripper28.com/7-cheap-and-fun-road-trips-to-take-from-minneapolis-this-weekend/\" target=\"_blank\"\u003eJennifer A Singer | DayTripper\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/figure\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eHere's the reality: the average American planning a summer vacation now expects to spend around $3,940 for flights and lodging. That's a lot of money, and it's making people think twice about expensive vacations far away. Instead, they're asking themselves: what can I do that doesn't cost as much?\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eMinnesota has a lot to offer. You've got the Twin Cities with museums, restaurants, and culture. Up north, you've got lakes and forests perfect for camping, fishing, and hiking. The North Shore along Lake Superior is stunning. You can kayak, swim, or just sit by the water. All of this is local, which means no expensive flights. Gas to drive there costs way less than plane tickets.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe state's tourism industry already pulled in \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.house.mn.gov/comm/docs/mWeFhAYs6kmSHHAePOQNsw.pdf\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003e$24.2 billion in economic impact\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e in 2023, and that number is growing. Hotels, restaurants, and attractions are benefiting from visitors who would normally go somewhere else entirely.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eWhat's driving this change? Rising costs everywhere are making people think smarter about vacations. Instead of flying to Europe or Hawaii, families are choosing road trips. Instead of fancy resorts, they're trying state parks and cabin rentals. And Minnesota is perfectly positioned because it's beautiful, varied, and affordable compared to other tourist destinations.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eLocal tourism businesses are ready for this shift. Small towns across Minnesota are hosting festivals, farmers markets, and outdoor events all summer long. Restaurants are celebrating local ingredients. Lodges and cabins are fully booked. This is what happens when people discover that great vacations don't always require leaving home.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThe best part? You can be a tourist in your own backyard. Minnesotans are exploring places they've never visited, and people from surrounding states are \u003c/span\u003e\u003ca href=\"https://www.nerdwallet.com/travel/studies/summer-travel-report\" rel=\"noopener\" class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__link\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003ediscovering Minnesota\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cspan\u003e for the first time.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\" dir=\"ltr\"\u003e\u003cspan\u003eThis summer, high travel costs might feel like a problem. But for Minnesota, it's an opportunity to show why this state is worth visiting—no plane ticket required.\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp class=\"NBAIEditor_Theme__paragraph\"\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cstyle style=\"display: none\"\u003e.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol1 {padding: 0 0 0 20px !important;margin: 0 0 24px 0 !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol2 {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;list-style-type: lower-alpha !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}html body.post #content-div .content ol li ol {margin: 0 !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol3 {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;list-style-type: lower-roman !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol4 {padding: 0;margin: 0;list-style-type: upper-roman !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ol5 {padding: 0;margin: 0;list-style-type: lower-roman !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul {padding: 0 !important;margin: 0 !important;margin-left: 20px !important;list-style-position: outside !important;}@media all and (max-width: 600px) {.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul {margin-left: 14px !important;}}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul li .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul li .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul li::before {display: none !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul {list-style-type: circle !important;margin-left: 0 !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__ul .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul .NBAIEditor_Theme__ul {list-style-type: square !important;margin-left: 0 !important;}html body.post #content-div .content ul li ul li ul {margin-left: 0 !important;}.ContentEditable__root \u003e ul {margin-bottom: 24px;padding: 0 0 0 20px;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__listItem {margin: 0 !important;padding: 0 !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__nestedListItem {list-style-type: none !important;padding: 0 0 0 24px !important;}.NBAIEditor_Theme__nestedListItem:before,.NBAIEditor_Theme__nestedListItem:after {display: none;